2. The probabilities of three teams, A, B, and C winning a volleyball competition are \frac{1}{4}, \frac{1}{8}, and \frac{1}{10} respectively. Assuming only one team can win, calculate the probability that; 
a) either A or B wins 
b) neither A nor C wins

Solution: 
\begin{align} 
a) P(A or B wins) &= P(A wins) + P(B wins) 
&= \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{8} 
&= \frac{2+1}{8} 
&= \frac{3}{8} 
\end{align} 
\begin{align} 
b) P(A or C wins) &= P(A wins) + P(C wins) 
&= \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{10} 
&= \frac{5+2}{20} 
&= \frac{7}{20} 
\end{align} 
